 >
 > I accept that there are wider issues but would like to think that LaTeX3
 > could address the general principle of providing aligned baselines
 > (perhaps as on option which can be switched on/off).
 >
In the general case, LaTeX *does* allow aligned baselines. its up to
the style designer to use fixed space, not variable bits of rubber,
between items. since TeX plonks rectangular boxes on the page very
precisely, its an ideal tool for building aligned baselines. I dont
quite see what the LaTeX 3 *kernel* needs to add. An example 2 column
style file with a good implementation of aligned baselines is
another matter, and it would be lovely to have it.

Sebastian



